2,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-15T22:31:30Z","updated_at":"2026-04-15T22:31:30Z","body":"This is likely a limitation of running through XWayland on GNOME, as GNOME on X11 never supported fractional scaling. KDE is the only desktop environment that supports fractional scaling on X11.\n\nmacOS performs similar trickery when using non-integer scale factors, which is unfortunately a performance hog, especially for 3D games.\n\n> If scaling is 100% or 200%, scaling works fine, full screen reports exactly your current screen resolution. Fullscreen (F11) should report your screen resolution. But 125% it will report 1.6x your resolution and 166% scaling it will report 1.2x resolution.\n\nThis checks out: `2.0 / 1.25 = 1.6` and `2.0 / 1.667 ~= 1.2` (where `2.0` is the 200% integer scale factor).\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4256084925/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]